        <param>
          <type>unsigned int</type>
          <declname>n</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Sets fast mode for computing the restraint. This mode only makes sense it the set_coarse_registration_mode option is false. This option only optimizes some coarse results (those given by the argument) to get the refined value. This option is very fast compared to a full optimization, and almost always is a good idea to use it with 1-5 results. This mode is still significantly slow compared to <ref refid="classIMP_1_1em2d_1_1Em2DRestraint_1a07c9060b33bc57a81e271fa4d16b64c5" kindref="member">set_coarse_registration_mode()</ref>, but the values optimized are optimum. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>n</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The number of images to optimize </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
